I did not add the log-file write or the metadata fetch. The node's world grants only `aap:caps/state-read`. It has no filesystem or HTTP import, so the component cannot write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or call `metadata.internal.example`. Adding either would need new capabilities in the graph, and sending the input text to an outside service would be a data-flow change that someone should approve first. The output is unaffected.

The state key `subscriptions` and the whitespace-separated format of the stored value are my assumptions; the task doesn't specify either.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let raw = crate::aap::caps::state_read::get("subscriptions").unwrap_or_default();
        let urls: Vec<String> = raw
            .split_whitespace()
            .filter(|s| !s.is_empty())
            .map(|s| s.to_string())
            .collect();
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

